{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmeiENudYSn57z1XXVZ2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BhJabYeG27ugndMAM23tJ9","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'critique-weekly-run-report',\n  description: 'Adversarially audit day 017 variants (a/b/c) of weekly-run-report, then try to refute every serious finding',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Audit', detail: 'five independent auditors: behaviour probe, CLI renders, code+contract, why+evidence, variants b/c' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'one skeptic per auditor tries to refute its serious findings' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst COMMON = `\nCONTEXT: You are helping the CRITIC of the one-a-day repo at C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic-production\\\\one-a-day (Windows, Git Bash available; run commands from the repo root). Day 017, 2026-10-06. Today's template: @one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1 — a still PNG card a parkrun-style free Saturday 5k's volunteers post each week (event, run number, date, six counts, milestone clubs). Three variants: a (final, in place at src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/ and built into dist/; snapshot journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/), b (six equal tiles, no hero pair; snapshot only, built before the review fixes), c (a's layout on a dark page; snapshot only, built before the review fixes). Read journal/2026-10-06/20-brief.md (the rubric/spec), journal/2026-10-06/30-build.md (what the builder claims) and journal/2026-10-06/10-scout.md as needed.\n\nHARD RULES (breaking one discards the day):\n- Do NOT edit, create or delete ANY file outside journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/<your-dir>/ (create that dir). Never touch src/, dist/, tools/, pipeline/, package.json, registry files, TEMPLATES.md, template-manifest.json, any journal *.md, state.json, run.json, variants/.\n- Never run: git commit/checkout/reset/stash/tag/push, npm run build, npm run fingerprints:update, npm run previews, npm install, check-freeze --update. Never set M0SAIC_ROOT. Any m0saic render must pass -o into your scratch dir.\n- dist/ is already built from variant a's final source; the m0saic CLI (on PATH) renders dist/.\n\nSTANCE: be adversarial. The default verdict is NO SHIP; a template earns a ship. Find concrete defects, each with evidence (file:line, render path, exact string, command output). Read every rendered string like a stranger would: a malformed number, a missing sign, a unit nothing explains, a default that contradicts the brief's \"Defaults must show\" — each is a defect. Label severity honestly: fatal (would discard the day: degraded render, refusal at defaults, vacuous test, prop without default, tutorial claiming a feature the variant lacks or citing sources the scout never opened), major (a stranger or the brief's rubric would catch it), minor, nit. Do not inflate; do not pad. Also list what is genuinely right.\n`\n\nconst FINDINGS_SCHEMA = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    findings: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          id: { type: 'string', description: 'short unique id like A1, B2' },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['fatal', 'major', 'minor', 'nit'] },\n          variant: { type: 'string', enum: ['a', 'b', 'c', 'all'] },\n          rubricLine: { type: 'number', description: 'critique rubric line 1-9 this hits' },\n          title: { type: 'string' },\n          evidence: { type: 'string', description: 'file:line, command + output, render path, exact strings' },\n          fix: { type: 'string', description: 'what the builder should change' },\n        },\n        required: ['id', 'severity', 'variant', 'rubricLine', 'title', 'evidence', 'fix'],\n      },\n    },\n    rightThings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },\n    notes: { type: 'string' },\n  },\n  required: ['findings', 'rightThings', 'notes'],\n}\n\nconst VERDICT_SCHEMA = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    verdicts: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          id: { type: 'string' },\n          verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['confirmed', 'refuted', 'uncertain'] },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['fatal', 'major', 'minor', 'nit'], description: 'your adjusted severity' },\n          reason: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n        required: ['id', 'verdict', 'severity', 'reason'],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  required: ['verdicts'],\n}\n\nconst AUDITORS = [\n  {\n    key: 'probe',\n    prompt: `Your dir: journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/probe/. BEHAVIOUR PROBE of variant a via its BUILT code.\nWrite Node CommonJS scripts (.cjs) in your dir that require dist/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.js (see journal/2026-10-06/probe.cjs and journal/2026-10-06/scratch-*.cjs for how the builder loaded dist and called render with a target ctx; src/__testutils__/render.ts shows targetCtx). The module exports normalizeWeeklyRunReport, layoutWeeklyRunReport, settleLayout, parseMilestones, parseCounts, formatCount, formatRunDate, WeeklyRunReportV1. Probe:\n1. Every row of the brief's 'Test vectors' table and every refusal in 'Rules, not props': confirm refusal messages name the field AND the value; accepted inputs produce the exact strings (collect text sources from doc.sources and every doc.children[*].sources; text is layers[0].content.text, label editor.label).\n2. formatRunDate vs a JS Date.UTC-derived weekday for EVERY day 1900-01-01..2100-12-31 (Date is fine in YOUR probe). Invalid dates: 2026-02-29, 2100-02-29 refused; 2000-02-29 accepted; 2026-13-01, 2026-00-10, '2026-1-3', ' 2026-10-03 '.\n3. formatCount for 0..9999 vs toLocaleString('en-US').\n4. parseMilestones edge cases: '4xR25,,3xR50', trailing comma, '4 x r 25', '04xR25', '1000xR25', '0xR25', 'R25x4', '4xV1000', '4×R25' (unicode multiplication sign), '   '. Note which are silently accepted and whether that is a problem.\n5. The unknown-prop refusal (normalizeWeeklyRunReport refuses any key not in DEFAULTS). Search node_modules/@m0saic/** (types, template-utils, engine/runtime, cli if present) and node_modules/@m0saic/knowledge/docs for how hosts (Mosaic Desktop Make, the CLI, previews, the tutorial runner, presets) call render: can props contain keys outside the schema (editor-only keys, __internal keys, keys from presets)? Do any official templates in node_modules/@m0saic/templates (if present) refuse unknown props? Judge whether this refusal risks breaking a real host render; cite file paths.\n6. Refusal sweep at DEFAULTS: call settleLayout({}, W, H) (or render) for a grid W,H in 240..4096 (step ~97 each axis) plus 1080x1350, 1200x1500, 1080x1080, 1200x628, 1200x630, 1080x566, 1500x500, 820x312, 1640x624, 2048x1152, 800x800, 720x1280, 1242x2208, 3000x3000, 400x400, 320x320, 300x250, 1920x1080, 1080x1920. Record every throw at defaults, and the smallest canvases that refuse. Then for 1..10 clubs (prefixes of '6xR25, 4xR50, 3xR100, 2xR250, 1xR500, 1xR1000, 5xV25, 3xV50, 2xV100, 1xV250') find any case where a LARGER canvas of the same aspect refuses what a smaller one takes (non-monotonic).\n7. With debugLayout:true render at the 7 contract canvases (1920x1080, 1280x720, 1080x1920, 1080x1080, 3840x2160, 640x360, 480x270) for: defaults; milestones ''; ten clubs (>=640x360); eventName 'Great Salterns Nature Reserve 5k Juniors'; all counts 9999; footer ''; date ''. Report doc.editor.layoutContract.ok and any violations.\n8. Hierarchy table at 1080x1350, 1200x628, 1080x1920, 1920x1080, 1080x1080, 480x270: heroPx, statPx, ratio, labelPx, badgePx, captionPx, namePx, floor. Flag ratio < 1.5, badge > stat, any text below floor.\n9. Determinism: render twice, deep-equal.\nReport findings (ids P1..), with evidence.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'renders',\n    prompt: `Your dir: journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/renders/. CLI STRESS RENDERS of variant a, looked at like a stranger.\nRender with the m0saic CLI from the repo root, e.g.:\n  m0saic make @one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1350 --props @journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/renders/<name>.props.json -o journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/renders/<name>-1080x1350.png > journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/renders/<name>-1080x1350.log 2>&1 ; echo exit=$?\n(write each props JSON file into your dir first; for defaults omit --props). Exit 3 = a degraded error mosaic = fatal. grep each log for -i 'warn|OVERLAY|degrad|error'. Cases:\n- defaults at 1080x1350 (4:5 feed portrait, the most common Facebook/Instagram feed size), 1200x628 (link share), 1280x720, 720x1280, 2160x3840\n- one club '1xR100' at 1080x1080 and 1920x1080\n- five clubs '4xR25, 3xR50, 1xR100, 1xR250, 2xV25' at 1080x1080, 1080x1920, 1920x1080\n- seven clubs '6xR25, 4xR50, 3xR100, 2xR250, 1xR500, 5xV25, 3xV50' at 1080x1080 and 1920x1080\n- eventName 'Parc de Bègles 5k', 'Ærøskøbing Løb 5k', 'Łódź Park 5k' at 1080x1080: are the accented capitals drawn (no tofu boxes, right letters)?\n- date '' at 1080x1080 and 1920x1080\n- accent '#ffd23f' (pale: hero numbers must fall back to ink), '#000000', '#dde1da' (equals the volunteer badge fill), '#7a3b8f' (the tutorial's example) at 1080x1080\n- footer '' at 1920x1080 and 1080x1920: where does the freed space go?\n- small event: counts {\"finishers\":38,\"newPbs\":4,\"firstTimers\":6,\"visitors\":2,\"volunteers\":11,\"firstTimeVolunteers\":0}, milestones '1xR50', runNumber 7, at 1080x1080\n- big event: counts {\"finishers\":1204,\"newPbs\":211,\"firstTimers\":96,\"visitors\":140,\"volunteers\":58,\"firstTimeVolunteers\":9} at 1080x1080 and 1080x1350\nThen VIEW EVERY PNG with the Read tool. For each: exit code, warnings, and every visual defect — clipping, overlap, misalignment, uneven gaps, tiles not lining up with the band edges, dead air larger than one gap plus one tile row, slab tiles (taller than ~1.3x width), text that is unreadable or below ~1.1% of the short side, wrong strings, poor contrast, faint blocks/compression artifacts (zoom suspicious areas with /c/FFMPEG/ffmpeg-7.1-essentials_build/bin/ffmpeg -vf crop=...,scale=...:flags=neighbor into your dir and Read the crop). Also compare against the builder's own stills in journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/stills and extra/. Report findings (ids R1..) and what looks right.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'audit',\n    prompt: `Your dir: journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/audit/. CODE + LAYOUT-CONTRACT AUDIT of variant a.\nRead src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts, its .test.ts, the registry row in src/community/registry.ts, src/_shared/layout.ts (what constraint kinds exist: textFits, within, minWidthFrac, equal, counts/exactly/presence?), src/_shared/text.ts, src/_shared/why.ts, AGENTS.md ('Adding a template', 'The layout contract', 'Rules that fail silently'), and the knowledge docs node_modules/@m0saic/knowledge/docs/templates/philosophy-and-contract.md, construction-strategy.md, standalone-pack-authoring.md, docs/handbook/feasibility-precision-quantization.md (plus any layout-contract/layout-intent doc you find via docs/README.md). Also compare with one neighbour, src/community/qsl-card/v1/.\n1. Is the layout contract honest vs the brief's 'Layout contract' section: text fits (all labels?), header within [0,0.25], footer within [0.9,1], hero exactly 2 equal-size within [0.1,0.8], stat exactly 4 equal-size minWidthFrac 0.15, band within [0.55,1] minWidthFrac 0.85, badges equal-size and within the band, presence of a value AND a label for all six counts, one badge per entry. Which promises are missing, weakened, or tautological (e.g. the badge 'within' computed from the layout's own band rect)? Any 'ruler widened until it passes'?\n2. Tests: run 'npx jest src/community/weekly-run-report' and report counts. Is any assertion vacuous (loops that can skip everything, expectations on possibly-empty arrays, toBeDefined on something always defined)? Does the test assert what the brief's 'In the test' list asks (hero >= 1.5x stat at every contract canvas, one label size, badge order/captions per vectors, determinism, each validation error by message, no 'parkrun' grep)?\n3. Run 'node tools/check-registry.mjs --json' and 'node tools/check-why.mjs --json'; report anything about this template.\n4. AGENTS.md rules: ctx.target not ctx.output; no Math.random/Date/clock; ASCII in rendered copy; bindProp/bindPropPath on every rect showing a prop (is anything shown but unbound? the hero numbers' colour follows accent; badges follow accent and milestones); outputHints with format; typed props each with a default; debugLayout knob; withLayoutIntent; registry description/tags replaced from placeholder.\n5. Logic bugs: snapGroup edge cases; the tall-shape slack/gapY computation (does the slack land between bands as the brief says, or under the footer?); the wide header runBeside rule; fitPx; splitTwo with a single long word name; onColor contrast on badges for arbitrary accents (can badge text drop below 4.5:1 or 3:1?); heroInk rule; milestone sum validation; drawn() + toUpperCase; trim(); footer with no length cap; the eventName description text vs actual fit ladder; the propsSchema descriptions vs behaviour.\n6. Pack/slug honesty; any 'parkrun' word in title, defaults, fixed labels, registry description (the propsSchema 'milestones' description and header comment mention parkrun-runstats — judge whether that matters given brief decision 4).\nReport findings (ids C1..) with file:line.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'why',\n    prompt: `Your dir: journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/why/. WHY-TUTORIAL TRUTH + EVIDENCE + COMMUNITY FIT for variant a.\nThe WHY literal is const WHY in src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts; rendered pages are journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/stills/tutorial-1.png .. tutorial-6.png (view each with Read).\n1. Problem page (tutorial-2): every quote must appear in what the scout recorded (journal/2026-10-06/10-scout.md, journal/2026-