. Which phases had run at build time? (The ship phase refreshes it; judge only whether the current one matches what had run.)\n5. Cover (tutorial-1): day 17, date, agent, model vs journal/2026-10-06/run.json and state.json.\n6. Community fit: with the sources plus a few WebSearch queries (e.g. 'parkrun run report facebook infographic', 'parkrun weekly results infographic powerpoint', 'parkrun event report template canva'), judge whether a run director or run-report writer would use this card instead of what they do now. What would stop them (counts as JSON in a form field, no importer, the milestone syntax, no photo, no event logo slot)? Are the milestone clubs right (parkrun run milestones 25/50/100/250/500/1000? volunteer milestones 25/50/100/250/500? any junior 11/21/50 clubs?) and does a results page or run report show 'first-time volunteers'? Cite links.\nReport findings (ids W1..) with evidence.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'bc',\n    prompt: `Your dir: journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/bc/. AUDIT OF VARIANTS b AND c (snapshots only; only a is built in dist, so judge b and c from stills, report.json and source).\nSnapshots: journal/2026-10-06/variants/b/ and journal/2026-10-06/variants/c/ (src/, stills/, renders/*.output.json, report.json). Variant a's final source: journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/src/. 30-build.md lists the review fixes made to a AFTER b and c were built.\n1. Diff b and c against a (git diff --no-index --stat and the relevant hunks) and list every behavioural difference, especially which review fixes b and c lack (unknown-prop refusal, club-count sanity, badge-vs-stat size, the rows rule for six clubs, mid-size canvas refusals, counts as a JSON string, footer cap, tutorial copy).\n2. View every still of b and c with Read (landscape, portrait, square, tutorial-1..6), string by string.\n3. Per variant: renders exit 0 / degraded false everywhere (report.json; also check renders/*.output.json for warnings such as OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP)? Do its defaults show what 20-brief.md 'Defaults must show' promised (b deliberately drops the hero pair; c changes the palette)? Does its tutorial-3 (solution page) describe THAT variant (does b still claim 'two numbers carry the week' or 'capped at 1/1.6'? does c?) — a solution page claiming a feature the variant lacks is fatal.\n4. Compute WCAG contrast for c's colours as read from c's source (page, ink, labels, tiles, accent, volunteer fill, badge text): tiles vs page, numbers vs tiles, labels vs tiles, badge text vs fills, footer vs page.\n5. Does b meet the brief's rubric item 1 (the week reads in two seconds; hero numbers >= 1.5x stat numbers)? Measure from b's stills/source.\n6. Do b's and c's tests assert things true for that variant?\nReport findings (ids V1..) with severity and variant, and in notes give three lines each for b and c: what is right, what is wrong, verdict.`,\n  },\n]\n\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  AUDITORS,\n  (a) => agent(COMMON + '\\n\\nYOUR TASK:\\n' + a.prompt, { label: `audit:${a.key}`, phase: 'Audit', schema: FINDINGS_SCHEMA }),\n  async (res, a) => {\n    if (!res) return { key: a.key, res: null, verdicts: [] }\n    const serious = res.findings.filter((f) => f.severity === 'fatal' || f.severity === 'major' || f.severity === 'minor')\n    if (serious.length === 0) return { key: a.key, res, verdicts: [] }\n    const v = await agent(\n      COMMON +\n        `\\n\\nYOUR TASK: You are a SKEPTIC. Another auditor (${a.key}) reported the findings below about today's template. For EACH finding, independently re-check the evidence yourself (open the files, rerun commands into journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/verify-${a.key}/, view images with Read) and try to REFUTE it: is it real, is it reproducible, is the severity right, is it already acknowledged in 30-build.md as a deliberate departure (still a defect if it breaks the brief's rubric, but say so)? Default to 'uncertain' if you cannot reproduce. Adjust severity up or down with a reason.\\n\\nFINDINGS:\\n` +\n        JSON.stringify(serious, null, 1),\n      { label: `verify:${a.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICT_SCHEMA },\n    )\n    return { key: a.key, res, verdicts: v ? v.verdicts : [] }\n  },\n)\nreturn results\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":175978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1218},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"281cba01-5109-4cf8-8e5b-19d8491f37d2","uuid":"138e8490-f0ad-4351-a48d-abfbfbece276","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:58:12.038Z","request_id":"req_011CfmeiE3ZPfgzfmztW9Yxy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BhJabYeG27ugndMAM23tJ9":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'critique-weekly-run-report',\n  description: 'Adversarially audit day 017 variants (a/b/c) of weekly-run-report, then try to refute every serious finding',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Audit', detail: 'five independent auditors: behaviour probe, CLI renders, code+contract, why+evidence, variants b/c' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'one skeptic per auditor tries to refute its serious findings' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst COMMON = `\nCONTEXT: You are helping the CRITIC of the one-a-day repo at C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic-production\\\\one-a-day (Windows, Git Bash available; run commands from the repo root). Day 017, 2026-10-06. Today's template: @one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1 — a still PNG card a parkrun-style free Saturday 5k's volunteers post each week (event, run number, date, six counts, milestone clubs). Three variants: a (final, in place at src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/ and built into dist/; snapshot journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/), b (six equal tiles, no hero pair; snapshot only, built before the review fixes), c (a's layout on a dark page; snapshot only, built before the review fixes). Read journal/2026-10-06/20-brief.md (the rubric/spec), journal/2026-10-06/30-build.md (what the builder claims) and journal/2026-10-06/10-scout.md as needed.\n\nHARD RULES (breaking one discards the day):\n- Do NOT edit, create or delete ANY file outside journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/<your-dir>/ (create that dir). Never touch src/, dist/, tools/, pipeline/, package.json, registry files, TEMPLATES.md, template-manifest.json, any journal *.md, state.json, run.json, variants/.\n- Never run: git commit/checkout/reset/stash/tag/push, npm run build, npm run fingerprints:update, npm run previews, npm install, check-freeze --update. Never set M0SAIC_ROOT. Any m0saic render must pass -o into your scratch dir.\n- dist/ is already built from variant a's final source; the m0saic CLI (on PATH) renders dist/.\n\nSTANCE: be adversarial. The default verdict is NO SHIP; a template earns a ship. Find concrete defects, each with evidence (file:line, render path, exact string, command output). Read every rendered string like a stranger would: a malformed number, a missing sign, a unit nothing explains, a default that contradicts the brief's \"Defaults must show\" — each is a defect. Label severity honestly: fatal (would discard the day: degraded render, refusal at defaults, vacuous test, prop without default, tutorial claiming a feature the variant lacks or citing sources the scout never opened), major (a stranger or the brief's rubric would catch it), minor, nit. Do not inflate; do not pad. Also list what is genuinely right.\n`\n\nconst FINDINGS_SCHEMA = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    findings: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          id: { type: 'string', description: 'short unique id like A1, B2' },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['fatal', 'major', 'minor', 'nit'] },\n          variant: { type: 'string', enum: ['a', 'b', 'c', 'all'] },\n          rubricLine: { type: 'number', description: 'critique rubric line 1-9 this hits' },\n          title: { type: 'string' },\n          evidence: { type: 'string', description: 'file:line, command + output, render path, exact strings' },\n          fix: { type: 'string', description: 'what the builder should change' },\n        },\n        required: ['id', 'severity', 'variant', 'rubricLine', 'title', 'evidence', 'fix'],\n      },\n    },\n    rightThings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },\n    notes: { type: 'string' },\n  },\n  required: ['findings', 'rightThings', 'notes'],\n}\n\nconst VERDICT_SCHEMA = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    verdicts: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          id: { type: 'string' },\n          verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['confirmed', 'refuted', 'uncertain'] },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['fatal', 'major', 'minor', 'nit'], description: 'your adjusted severity' },\n          reason: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n        required: ['id', 'verdict', 'severity', 'reason'],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  required: ['verdicts'],\n}\n\nconst AUDITORS = [\n  {\n    key: 'probe',\n    prompt: `Your dir: journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/probe/. BEHAVIOUR PROBE of variant a via its BUILT code.\nWrite Node CommonJS scripts (.cjs) in your dir that require dist/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.js (see journal/2026-10-06/probe.cjs and journal/2026-10-06/scratch-*.cjs for how the builder loaded dist and called render with a target ctx; src/__testutils__/render.ts shows targetCtx). The module exports normalizeWeeklyRunReport, layoutWeeklyRunReport, settleLayout, parseMilestones, parseCounts, formatCount, formatRunDate, WeeklyRunReportV1. Probe:\n1. Every row of the brief's 'Test vectors' table and every refusal in 'Rules, not props': confirm refusal messages name the field AND the value; accepted inputs prod