.3x width), text that is unreadable or below ~1.1% of the short side, wrong strings, poor contrast, faint blocks/compression artifacts (zoom suspicious areas with /c/FFMPEG/ffmpeg-7.1-essentials_build/bin/ffmpeg -vf crop=...,scale=...:flags=neighbor into your dir and Read the crop). Also compare against the builder's own stills in journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/stills and extra/. Report findings (ids R1..) and what looks right.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'audit',\n    prompt: `Your dir: journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/audit/. CODE + LAYOUT-CONTRACT AUDIT of variant a.\nRead src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts, its .test.ts, the registry row in src/community/registry.ts, src/_shared/layout.ts (what constraint kinds exist: textFits, within, minWidthFrac, equal, counts/exactly/presence?), src/_shared/text.ts, src/_shared/why.ts, AGENTS.md ('Adding a template', 'The layout contract', 'Rules that fail silently'), and the knowledge docs node_modules/@m0saic/knowledge/docs/templates/philosophy-and-contract.md, construction-strategy.md, standalone-pack-authoring.md, docs/handbook/feasibility-precision-quantization.md (plus any layout-contract/layout-intent doc you find via docs/README.md). Also compare with one neighbour, src/community/qsl-card/v1/.\n1. Is the layout contract honest vs the brief's 'Layout contract' section: text fits (all labels?), header within [0,0.25], footer within [0.9,1], hero exactly 2 equal-size within [0.1,0.8], stat exactly 4 equal-size minWidthFrac 0.15, band within [0.55,1] minWidthFrac 0.85, badges equal-size and within the band, presence of a value AND a label for all six counts, one badge per entry. Which promises are missing, weakened, or tautological (e.g. the badge 'within' computed from the layout's own band rect)? Any 'ruler widened until it passes'?\n2. Tests: run 'npx jest src/community/weekly-run-report' and report counts. Is any assertion vacuous (loops that can skip everything, expectations on possibly-empty arrays, toBeDefined on something always defined)? Does the test assert what the brief's 'In the test' list asks (hero >= 1.5x stat at every contract canvas, one label size, badge order/captions per vectors, determinism, each validation error by message, no 'parkrun' grep)?\n3. Run 'node tools/check-registry.mjs --json' and 'node tools/check-why.mjs --json'; report anything about this template.\n4. AGENTS.md rules: ctx.target not ctx.output; no Math.random/Date/clock; ASCII in rendered copy; bindProp/bindPropPath on every rect showing a prop (is anything shown but unbound? the hero numbers' colour follows accent; badges follow accent and milestones); outputHints with format; typed props each with a default; debugLayout knob; withLayoutIntent; registry description/tags replaced from placeholder.\n5. Logic bugs: snapGroup edge cases; the tall-shape slack/gapY computation (does the slack land between bands as the brief says, or under the footer?); the wide header runBeside rule; fitPx; splitTwo with a single long word name; onColor contrast on badges for arbitrary accents (can badge text drop below 4.5:1 or 3:1?); heroInk rule; milestone sum validation; drawn() + toUpperCase; trim(); footer with no length cap; the eventName description text vs actual fit ladder; the propsSchema descriptions vs behaviour.\n6. Pack/slug honesty; any 'parkrun' word in title, defaults, fixed labels, registry description (the propsSchema 'milestones' description and header comment mention parkrun-runstats — judge whether that matters given brief decision 4).\nReport findings (ids C1..) with file:line.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'why',\n    prompt: `Your dir: journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/why/. WHY-TUTORIAL TRUTH + EVIDENCE + COMMUNITY FIT for variant a.\nThe WHY literal is const WHY in src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts; rendered pages are journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/stills/tutorial-1.png .. tutorial-6.png (view each with Read).\n1. Problem page (tutorial-2): every quote must appear in what the scout recorded (journal/2026-10-06/10-scout.md, journal/2026-10-06/scout-notes/*.md) AND in the real source. Fetch the four source URLs with WebFetch (load it via ToolSearch 'select:WebFetch'; GitHub READMEs are at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/<owner>/<repo>/HEAD/README.md, also try main/master). Verify each quote verbatim. Check rwkura/parkrun-milestones: does it really 'print the stats of the latest run in list format'? What are its exact output lines (parkrunners, New PBs, Visitors, First-time parkrunners, Volunteers, First-time volunteers, Milestones: 4xR25...)? Is the separator an ASCII 'x' or '×'? Does it print volunteer milestones at all? Is 'Both stop at text; the one infographic lives inside the results page' fair to ear1grey's extension and Eventuate?\n2. Solution page (tutorial-3): every claim must hold for variant a's code. Check 'numbers capped at 1/1.6 of the headline size', 'milestones line in its own syntax (4xR25, plus V for volunteer clubs)', 'empty week says so and keeps the shape', 'No parkrun name, logo or colours', caveat 'Six to ten clubs take two rows of smaller badges (one long row on a thumbnail)', caveat 'On a thumbnail such as 480x270, seven or more clubs may be refused'. For the last two write a small .cjs probe in your dir that requires dist/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.js (see journal/2026-10-06/probe.cjs) and calls settleLayout(props, 480, 270) for 6..10 clubs with default counts and with long captions (two/three-digit counts) — is the caveat accurate?\n3. Use-it page (tutorial-4): would the command work as written? Is the example accent '#7a3b8f' (a purple) at odds with the brief's decision 4 (no parkrun lookalike palette; parkrun's brand uses a purple and an apricot — look up parkrun's brand purple hex with WebSearch)? Is 'numbers stay ink if it reads poorly' true in code? Is the week.json example ('counts':{...}) a fair placeholder?\n4. Timeline page (tutorial-6): run 'node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/2026-10-06/trace.json' and compare with WHY.timeline. Which phases had run at build time? (The ship phase refreshes it; judge only whether the current one matches what had run.)\n5. Cover (tutorial-1): day 17, date, agent, model vs journal/2026-10-06/run.json and state.json.\n6. Community fit: with the sources plus a few WebSearch queries (e.g. 'parkrun run report facebook infographic', 'parkrun weekly results infographic powerpoint', 'parkrun event report template canva'), judge whether a run director or run-report writer would use this card instead of what they do now. What would stop them (counts as JSON in a form field, no importer, the milestone syntax, no photo, no event logo slot)? Are the milestone clubs right (parkrun run milestones 25/50/100/250/500/1000? volunteer milestones 25/50/100/250/500? any junior 11/21/50 clubs?) and does a results page or run report show 'first-time volunteers'? Cite links.\nReport findings (ids W1..) with evidence.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'bc',\n    prompt: `Your dir: journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/bc/. AUDIT OF VARIANTS b AND c (snapshots only; only a is built in dist, so judge b and c from stills, report.json and source).\nSnapshots: journal/2026-10-06/variants/b/ and journal/2026-10-06/variants/c/ (src/, stills/, renders/*.output.json, report.json). Variant a's final source: journal/2026-10-06/variants/a/src/. 30-build.md lists the review fixes made to a AFTER b and c were built.\n1. Diff b and c against a (git diff --no-index --stat and the relevant hunks) and list every behavioural difference, especially which review fixes b and c lack (unknown-prop refusal, club-count sanity, badge-vs-stat size, the rows rule for six clubs, mid-size canvas refusals, counts as a JSON string, footer cap, tutorial copy).\n2. View every still of b and c with Read (landscape, portrait, square, tutorial-1..6), string by string.\n3. Per variant: renders exit 0 / degraded false everywhere (report.json; also check renders/*.output.json for warnings such as OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP)? Do its defaults show what 20-brief.md 'Defaults must show' promised (b deliberately drops the hero pair; c changes the palette)? Does its tutorial-3 (solution page) describe THAT variant (does b still claim 'two numbers carry the week' or 'capped at 1/1.6'? does c?) — a solution page claiming a feature the variant lacks is fatal.\n4. Compute WCAG contrast for c's colours as read from c's source (page, ink, labels, tiles, accent, volunteer fill, badge text): tiles vs page, numbers vs tiles, labels vs tiles, badge text vs fills, footer vs page.\n5. Does b meet the brief's rubric item 1 (the week reads in two seconds; hero numbers >= 1.5x stat numbers)? Measure from b's stills/source.\n6. Do b's and c's tests assert things true for that variant?\nReport findings (ids V1..) with severity and variant, and in notes give three lines each for b and c: what is right, what is wrong, verdict.`,\n  },\n]\n\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  AUDITORS,\n  (a) => agent(COMMON + '\\n\\nYOUR TASK:\\n' + a.prompt, { label: `audit:${a.key}`, phase: 'Audit', schema: FINDINGS_SCHEMA }),\n  async (res, a) => {\n    if (!res) return { key: a.key, res: null, verdicts: [] }\n    const serious = res.findings.filter((f) => f.severity === 'fatal' || f.severity === 'major' || f.severity === 'minor')\n    if (serious.length === 0) return { key: a.key, res, verdicts: [] }\n    const v = await agent(\n      COMMON +\n        `\\n\\nYOUR TASK: You are a SKEPTIC. Another auditor (${a.key}) reported the findings below about today's template. For EACH finding, independently re-check the evidence yourself (open the files, rerun commands into journal/2026-10-06/critique-scratch/verify-${a.key}/, view images with Read) and try to REFUTE it: is it real, is it reproducible, is the severity right, is it already acknowledged in 30-build.md as a deliberate departure (still a defect if it breaks the brief's rubric, but say so)? Default to 'uncertain' if you cannot reproduce. Adjust severity up or down with a reason.\\n\\nFINDINGS:\\n` +\n        JSON.stringify(serious, null, 1),\n      { label: `verify:${a.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICT_SCHEMA },\n    )\n    return { key: a.key, res, verdicts: v ? v.verdicts : [] }\n  },\n)\nreturn results\n","uuid":"86c20352-a864-43f7-9082-dfcc0313fdfe","session_id":"281cba01-5109-4cf8-8e5b-19d8491f37d2"}
